      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Annihilation Aura",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "aura",
        "emotion",
        "mental"
      ],
      "text": "20 feet. The Carcass Man's form exudes the impulse to destroy. Upon entering the aura, creatures must attempt a DC 31 Will save save. Regardless of the results, creatures are temporarily immune for 1 minute.\n\n---\nCritical Success The creature is unaffected.\n\nSuccess Urges to attack cloud the creature's mind and if they do not deal damage to another creature on their turn, they become Stupefied 1 until the end of their next turn.\n\nFailure The creature is Confused until the end of their next turn.\n\nCritical Failure The creature is confused for 1 minute.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "unsupported",
          "foundry": {
            "key": "Aura",
            "radius": 20,
            "traits": [
              "emotion",
              "mental"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Reactive Strike",
      "actions": "reaction",
      "category": "defensive"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Neck Snap",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Requirements The Carcass Man has a creature Grabbed\n\n---\nEffect The creature takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 31 basic Fortitude save save); a creature that critically fails their save is Paralyzed until they heal at least 30 HP. The Carcass Man then releases the creature."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Revel in Destruction",
      "actions": "free",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "divine",
        "emotion",
        "fear",
        "mental",
        "visual"
      ],
      "text": "Requirements The Carcass Man's last action reduced a creature to 0 HP\n\n---\nEffect The Carcass Man exults in his victory, painting his face in the creature's blood. He is Quickened until the end of his next turn but can use this extra action only to Strike. Non-worshippers of Zagresh who witness the display must succeed at a DC 31 Will save save or be Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Three-Arm Devastation",
      "actions": 3,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The Carcass Man attempts a melee Strike against a creature within his reach. If the Strike hits and deals damage, he can attempt two additional melee Strikes with his other arms against two other creatures within his reach; each of the three Strikes must target a different creature. These attacks increase his multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until all three attacks have been made."
    },
